  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on skewness, specifically preferring the lottery that is more left-skewed, meaning a higher concentration of probability on relatively favorable outcomes. To assess skewness in this context, we must compare the distribution of probabilities across favorable vs. unfavorable outcomes for each lottery. In this decision problem, both lotteries involve only zero or negative outcomes (losses or nothing), so 'favorable' outcomes must be interpreted as less negative (i.e., closer to zero). Lottery A has a 55% chance of 0 Euros (favorable) and 45% chance of -6000 (unfavorable). Lottery B has a 10% chance of 0 Euros (favorable) and 90% chance of -3000 (unfavorable). Thus, the probability mass on favorable outcomes is 55% for A and 10% for B. Therefore, Lottery A assigns a greater portion of probability to favorable outcomes and is more left-skewed. According to the decision reason, Lottery A should be preferred.",
